WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.720
Angie Juban: Since you did home management as a student at LSU and then you were sort of a student,

2
00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:13.420
sort of an instructor at [the University of] Tennessee, what were the differences between LSU’s program and the Tennessee program?

3
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:13.927
A.B.

4
00:00:13.927 --> 00:00:23.840
Clark: I think basically they were pretty much the same.

5
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:30.020
Students lived in a group situation, small group situation,

6
00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:40.920
and determined what kinds of jobs needed to be done to run a household and then divided those into categories and you were,

7
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:46.840
you know . . . like gave a name to each one of those categories and then you shifted from one category to the next.

8
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:57.320
You were like the hostess, or the cook, or the maid, or whatever for so many weeks or days or something like that.

9
00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.300
I think the difference in the program at Tennessee and at LSU basically,

10
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:08.260
they had babies in the houses in Tennessee, which we did not have at LSU.

11
00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:14.140
They would get them from the welfare department and they would be in the house.

12
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:19.820
That was a major role which we did not have at LSU.

13
00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:26.620
They did away with that pretty quickly, because it just was difficult . . . but it was a good experience for the girls,

14
00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:31.700
to have a baby and know that they cry and they are demanding.
